@hyukjlee  

can we stick to `--monokernel `instead of `VLLM_ROCM_MONO_DECODE=1 `? 
@Fangzhou-Ai  dsv4.1f may need a patch for this

==
On the switch: `guards.enabled()` accepts both `--monokernel` and `VLLM_ROCM_MONO_DECODE=1`. RFC #60904 asks for a single switch with no other user knobs. Could you either drop the `VLLM_ROCM_MONO_DECODE` alias from the `common/mono` path, or keep it and document it as deprecated in favor of `--monokernel`? For the second option, that would mean a deprecation warning when the env var enables a `MonoSpec` model, plus a note in `envs.py` and the README.
